<%# locals: (token:) %>
<%# A keyboard or screen-reader user gets no other signal this appeared: the
    stream that inserts it destroys the focused Create-token submit button, and
    role="status"/"alert" alone isn't announced reliably (project lesson,
    2026-09-25 profile-tokens review). autofocus moves focus here instead —
    the controller orders this stream action AFTER the form/list replace so
    there's nothing already focused for it to lose to — and aria-describedby
    ties the one-time warning to the element that receives it. %>
<%# The wrapper carries THIS token's id (dom_id(token, :reveal)), not a fixed
    "api-token-reveal" — the div of that fixed id lives in _section.html.erb
    and only ever holds one token's reveal at a time, replaced wholesale on
    create. Revoking an older token B must not touch a newer token A's
    freshly-shown reveal, so the controller's destroy targets this id
    specifically (turbo_stream.remove) rather than emptying the fixed
    container: a remove for an id that isn't currently on the page is a
    silent no-op, exactly what's wanted when B's reveal isn't showing. %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(token, :reveal) %>" data-turbo-temporary>
  <div class="card" data-controller="clipboard" data-turbo-temporary style="margin-block: var(--space-4);">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p id="api-token-reveal-warning"><strong>Copy your new token now.</strong> This is the only time TurboFlows will show it.</p>
      <code class="api-token-reveal__code" data-clipboard-target="source"><%= token.plaintext %></code>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-action="click->clipboard#copy"
              data-clipboard-target="button" autofocus aria-describedby="api-token-reveal-warning">Copy</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= render "profiles/api_tokens/connect", token:, base_url: request.base_url %>
</div>
